\par\par \uc2 Foreign Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 2 Major Chains Prepare to Sell  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pills\b0\par\par\uc2 By Pam Belluck \par \uc2 1,278 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 March 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The pill mifepristone will be available with a prescription at pharmacy counters in a few states to start.\par \par \uc2 The two largest pharmacy chains in the United States will start dispensing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill mifepristone this month, a step that could make access easier for some patients.\par \par \uc2 Officials at CVS and \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  said in interviews on Friday that they had received certification to dispense mifepristone under guidelines that the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  issued last year. The chains plan to make the medication available in stores in a handful of states at first. They will not be providing the medication by mail.\par \par \uc2 Both chains said they would gradually expand to all other states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was legal and where pharmacies were legally able to dispense \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills -- about half of the states.\par \par \uc2 President Biden said in a statement on Friday that the availability of the pill at pharmacies was ''an important milestone in ensuring access to mifepristone, a drug that has been approved by the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  as safe and effective for more than 20 years.''\par \par \uc2 ''I encourage all pharmacies that want to pursue this option to seek certification,'' he added.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  will start providing the pill within the next week in a small number of its pharmacies in New York, Pennsylvania, Massachusetts, California and Illinois, said Fraser Engerman, a spokesman for the chain. ''We are beginning a phased rollout in select locations to allow us to ensure quality, safety and privacy for our patients, providers and team members,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 CVS will begin dispensing in all of its pharmacies in Massachusetts and Rhode Island ''in the weeks ahead,'' Amy Thibault, a spokeswoman for the company, said.\par \par \uc2 The chains will be monitoring the prospects in a few states, including Kansas, Montana and Wyoming, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or strict limitations have been enacted but are enjoined because of legal challenges.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Engerman said that \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  was ''not going to dispense in states where the laws are unclear'' to protect its pharmacists and staff members.\par \par \uc2 As for CVS, ''we continually monitor and evaluate changes in state laws and will dispense mifepristone in any state where it is or becomes legally permissible to do so,'' Ms. Thibault said. In some states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, she said, pharmacists are prohibited from dispensing mifepristone because laws require that to be done by doctors or in a hospital or clinic.\par \par \uc2 It is uncertain how much initial demand there will be for the service at brick-and-mortar pharmacies. In the states where the chains will begin dispensing, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills are already available in clinics or easily prescribed through telemedicine and sent through the mail. But some women prefer to visit doctors, many of whom do not have the medication on hand. The new development will allow doctors and other eligible providers to send a prescription to a pharmacy for the patient to pick up.\par \par \uc2 ''Now that doctors no longer have to stock the medicine themselves and dispense it, it increases the likelihood that a patient can go to their own doctor, the person with whom they already have a relationship, and say, 'I'm pregnant -- I don't want to be,''' said Kirsten Moore, the director of the Expanding Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Access Project.\par \par \uc2 She said it might also motivate more doctors and other health providers to obtain the special certification that the F.D.A. requires for prescribers of mifepristone. The steps to becoming a certified prescriber are simple, but some doctors have been deterred because of the paperwork and logistics of having to order and stock the pills.\par \par \uc2 As the availability in retail pharmacies expands, they may become a more popular alternative, and depending on the outcome of a case the Supreme Court will hear later this month, the pharmacy option could take on more importance.\par \par \uc2 In that case, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have sued the F.D.A., seeking to remove mifepristone from the market in the United States. An appeals court ruling in that case did not go that far but effectively banned the mailing of mifepristone and required in-person doctor visits. If the Supreme Court upholds that ruling, it could mean that patients would have to obtain mifepristone by visiting a clinic or doctor. If such a ruling allowed pharmacies to continue dispensing, more patients might obtain the medication there.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents criticized the pharmacy chains' decision. ''As two of the world's largest, most trusted 'health' brands, the decision by CVS and \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  to sell dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs is shameful, and the harm to unborn babies and their mothers incalculable,'' Katie Daniel, the state policy director of Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In order to obtain certification, the pharmacy chains had to take specific steps, including ensuring that their computerized systems protected the privacy of prescribers, who are certified under a special program that the F.D.A. applies to mifepristone and several dozen other medications.\par \par \uc2 Pharmacy certification is granted by manufacturers of mifepristone. \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  was certified by the brand name manufacturer Danco Laboratories, and is seeking certification from the generic manufacturer GenBioPro, Mr. Engerman said. CVS was certified by GenBioPro.\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a two-drug regimen that is now the most common method of terminating pregnancies in the United States and is typically used through 12 weeks of pregnancy. Mifepristone, which blocks a hormone necessary for pregnancy development, is taken first, followed 24 to 48 hours later by misoprostol, which causes contractions that expel pregnancy tissue.\par \par \uc2 The same regimen is also used for miscarriages, and those patients can now also obtain mifepristone from the pharmacy chains.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone has been tightly regulated by the F.D.A. since its approval in 2000. It had previously been available primarily from the prescribers or from clinics or telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, in which the pills were generally shipped from one of two mail-order pharmacies that were authorized. Misoprostol has never been as tightly restricted as mifepristone and is used for many different medical conditions. It is easily obtained at pharmacies through a typical prescription process.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American Pharmacists Association\uc2  urged the F.D.A. to allow retail pharmacies to distribute mifepristone, even though the medication is unlikely to generate significant revenue. In a statement last year, the association said that it wanted the agency ''to level the playing field by permitting any pharmacy that chooses to dispense this product to become certified.''\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the F.D.A. policy change was announced in January 2023, \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  and CVS said they planned to become certified and offer mifepristone in states where laws would allow pharmacies to dispense it.\par \par \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  later became the focus of a consumer and political firestorm after it responded to threatening letters from Republican attorneys general in 21 states, confirming that it would not dispense the medication in those states.\par \par \uc2 Both chains have had protests outside their stores, mostly from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates, and similar protesters interrupted a meeting of shareholders at \uc2 Walgreens Boots Alliance\uc2 , the chain's parent company.\par \par \uc2 CVS is the nation's largest chain with over 9,000 stores in all 50 states. \uc2 Walgreens\uc2  has about 8,500 stores in all states except North Dakota. Neither chain would discuss the price of the medication, but both noted that some insurance policies would cover it in some states.\par \par \uc2 A handful of small independent pharmacies began dispensing mifepristone last year.\par \par \uc2 The pill mifepristone will be available with a prescription at Walgreens and CVS pharmacy counters in a few states to start. (PHOTOGRAPH BY ANNA MONEYMAKER/GETTY IMAGES) (A18) This article appeared in print on page A1, A18. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240302ek320002x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
