\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Women Who Are Not Pregnant Are Requesting  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Pills, Just in Case\b0\par\par\uc2 By Pam Belluck \par \uc2 769 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 January 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 11\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The News\par \par \uc2 Tens of thousands of women who are not pregnant are ordering \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills just in case they might need them someday, especially in states where access is threatened, according to a study published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Why It Matters\par \par \uc2 The practice, known as advance provision, is relatively new and has increased significantly since the Supreme Court's decision in 2022 to overturn the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the study, published in the journal JAMA Internal Medicine, researchers evaluated data from Aid Access, a telehealth organization that has long provided \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to women in the first 13 weeks of pregnancy and began offering the medication to women in the United States who weren't pregnant in September 2021.\par \par \uc2 Before May 2022, when a draft of the Supreme Court decision was leaked, Aid Access had received about 6,000 advance provision requests, averaging 25 per day. Since then, it has received over 42,000 requests, averaging 118 per day, said Dr. Abigail Aiken, an associate professor at the \uc2 University of Texas at Austin\uc2  and a co-author of the study.\par \par \uc2 The biggest spikes in demand followed events that raised doubts about the future availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Requests peaked in the weeks between the leak and the Supreme Court's decision in June 2022, and in April 2023 after a flurry of court rulings in a lawsuit by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents seeking to curtail mifepristone, a key \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill, a case now before the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Rates of requests were highest in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans were expected -- even higher than in states that already had bans. Asked why they requested the pills, most women said to ''ensure personal health and choice'' and ''prepare for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions,'' according to the study.\par \par \uc2 ''People were obviously paying attention and seeing the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access either going away or being reduced where they were and thinking, 'I need to get prepared for that,''' Dr. Aiken said.\par \par \uc2 Behind the Numbers\par \par \uc2 Data from September 2021 through April 2023 showed 48,404 advance provision requests and 147,112 requests from women seeking to terminate existing pregnancies. (Women in both categories completed telehealth consultations and Aid Access evaluated their medical information before prescribing pills.)\par \par \uc2 Advance provision requesters were more likely than those already pregnant to be 30 or older, white and childless, and to live in urban neighborhoods with lower poverty rates than the national average. That might be partly because Aid Access offers free or reduced-price services to pregnant patients who need financial assistance, while advance provision requesters were expected to pay the full $110 cost, Dr. Aiken said.\par \par \uc2 And because few organizations offer advance provision, women from marginalized or lower-income communities might be less aware ''that it's even a thing you can do,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 Medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically involves two pills: mifepristone, which has a shelf life of three to five years, followed a day or two later by misoprostol, which has a shelf life of 18 to 24 months.\par \par \uc2 Dr. Aiken said a subset of advance provision requesters -- 937 women, two-thirds of them in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans or restrictions -- answered follow-up questions. Most still had the pills, but 58 had taken them and 55 had given them to someone else.\par \par \uc2 About 60 percent took the pills before seven weeks of pregnancy, early in the recommended time frame. A vast majority reported having enough information, including about expected bleeding and cramping. All 58 said the pills worked. Five visited health care providers afterward, but none went to the hospital or had serious complications.\par \par \uc2 Larger Implications\par \par \uc2 Legal scholars say advance provision may be legal in some states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. ''Many state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws require a provider to know a person is pregnant,'' three law professors -- David S. Cohen, Greer Donley and Rachel Rebouch\u233\'00\'E9 -- wrote in an article to be published in the Stanford Law Review. However, they added, in some states, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers might be legally vulnerable since they know that ''the pills are prescribed to terminate a future pregnancy.''\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents object to advance provision and claim \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication is dangerous. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters say prescribing it in case of future need, like antibiotics for traveler's diarrhea, increases access and underscores that the pills are safe, as many studies show.\par \par \uc2 Advance requests for \uc2  pills like mifepristone peaked shortly after a draft of the Supreme Court decision to overturn Roe v. Wade was leaked. (PHOTOGRAPH BY EVELYN HOCKSTEIN/REUTERS) This article appeared in print on page A11. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240103ek1300043\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
